## MLflow example

`resources/example_ml.*.yml` define a serverless job that trains a PyTorch
room-availability model on synthetic bookings, registers it in Unity Catalog
with a `padda` alias, and scores the coming week in batch. Code lives in
`src/{{template `package_name` .}}/ml/`, tests in `tests/test_ml_*.py`.

Compute has no internet access, so run `scripts/upload_ml_wheels.sh <target> <profile>`
once after the first `databricks bundle deploy` to put torch and its
dependencies on the bundle's wheels volume. The optional serving endpoint in
`resources/optional/` is documented in the platform guide
"Publisere modell som serving-endepunkt".

{{end -}}
