## Freshness alert

`resources/freshness_alert.job.yml` defines a scheduled serverless job that
checks when each watched table last received new data. If that is longer ago
than the table's freshness threshold, or the table cannot be checked, the job
fails and the failure notification goes to Slack. The daily 07:00 schedule is
paused by default, so the job only runs when started; set `pause_status` to
`UNPAUSED` under `schedule` in that file to run it on the schedule, and change
the cron expression to run it at other times.
Watched tables are listed as job parameters in the same file; replace the
generated entry with your own tables. Code lives in
`src/{{template `package_name` .}}/freshness/`, tests in `tests/test_freshness.py`.

Set the name of the Slack notification destination under `slack_destination_id`
for each target in `databricks.yml` before the first `databricks bundle deploy`;
validate and deploy fail while it is `REPLACE_WITH_DESTINATION_NAME`.
See the platform guide
"[Sette opp ferskhetsvarsel](https://padda.data.oslo.systems/guider/overvaake-og-drifte/ferskhetsvarsel/)".

